MT6797 SDR104 AutoK
===================

The MSDC1 SD tuning path retains the previously deployed scan counts, tuning
commands, latch checks, failure handling and window selection. It uses its own
small controller context and explicit MMIO helpers. The raw access and full
post-write barrier match the previous BSP integration. eMMC HS400 tuning remains
in mtk-sd.c and does not use this SD implementation.

analysis.c contains the controller-independent 64-bit scan scoring, bounded
boundary parser and edge/delay selection. test-mt6797-autok-analysis.py compares
these functions with the P10 production version, including rejected inputs.
The obsolete offline and AutoK eMMC/SDIO paths are omitted. Tuning results are
reapplied on clock changes and cleared on card power-off. The adapter restores
PIO and propagates failures to MMC core. Routine tuning diagnostics are debug
only; failed SDR104 tuning remains an error.
